ont-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">Your budget stops at about $350</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want 88 weighted keys, not a 61-key keyboard</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You mostly play chords, pop songs or with an app</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#1f7a4d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2713</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want to try piano before spending more</span></div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:20px 22px;background:#fdf3f0\"><div style=\"font-size:26px;font-weight:800;color:#b0442d;margin-bottom:6px\">Skip it if\u2026</div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">Piano sound really matters to you</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You plan to practice every day for years</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You play classical pieces with lots of dynamics</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You want Bluetooth for apps or music</span></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #d9e2e5\"><span style=\"flex:none;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:#b0442d;color:#fff;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:800\">\u2715</span><span style=\"font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.4\">You can stretch to about $500 (get the P-145BT)</span></div></div></div><div class=\"foot\"><span>Pianoers.com \u00b7 Alesis Recital Pro MKII review</span><b>PIANOERS.COM</b></div></body></html>"], "alesis-recital-pro-mkii-accessories": [590, "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@500;700;800&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,500;1,500&family=Noto+Music&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0}\nbody{width:1200px;height:590px;font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif;background:#f3f6f7;color:#15191c;padding:52px 60px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}\n.eyebrow{font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2e6475}\nh1{font-size:48px;line-height:1.05;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:8px 0 26px}\n.foot{position:absolute;left:60px;right:60px;bottom:20px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:17px;color:#56666e;font-weight:500}\n.foot b{letter-spacing:.12em;color:#2e6475}\n.card{background:#fff;border:1px solid #d9e2e5;border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(21 25 28/6%),0 8px 24px rgb(21 25 28/6%)}\nsvg text{font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif}\n.mus{font-family:\"Noto Music\",serif}\n</style></head><body><div class=\"eyebrow\">Complete the setup</div><h1>What to buy with the Recital Pro MKII</h1><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px\"><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">SUSTAIN PEDAL</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;white-space:nowrap;background:#fff3d1;color:#8a5a00\">Upgrade first</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Piano-style pedal</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">The included pedal is a small square footswitch that slides around. A piano-shaped pedal such as the Alesis ASP-2 feels far more natural.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">STAND</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;white-space:nowrap;background:#fff3d1;color:#8a5a00\">Needed</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">X-style keyboard stand</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">No stand in the box. Alesis says any standard X-type stand works, no screws needed.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">BENCH</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;white-space:nowrap;background:#fff3d1;color:#8a5a00\">Needed</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Adjustable bench</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">Forearms level with the keys. A kitchen chair is usually too low.</div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"padding:16px 18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\"><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#2e6475\">HEADPHONES</span><span style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:800;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px;white-space:nowrap;background:#e2eef1;color:#2e6475\">Useful</span></div><div style=\"font-size:21px;font-weight:800\">Any wired pair</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-family:Lora,serif;color:#33424a;line-height:1.4\">The front jack is 1/8-inch. Use plain headphones: ones with a mic and buttons can sound wrong.</div></div></div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:16px;padding:14px 20px;font-size:17px\">The box includes the piano, a music rest, the power adapter and the footswitch pedal.</div><div class=\"foot\"><span>Pianoers.com \u00b7 Alesis Recital Pro MKII review</span><b>PIANOERS.COM</b></div></body></html>"], "alesis-recital-pro-mkii-rear-panel": [800, "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Schibsted+Grotesk:wght@500;700;800&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,500;1,500&family=Noto+Music&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0}\nbody{width:1200px;height:800px;font-family:\"Schibsted Grotesk\",Arial,sans-serif;background:#f3f6f7;color:#15191c;padding:52px 60px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden}\n.eyebrow{font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spac